			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1434077">
									

<p>&#8230; you <em>didn't know</em> about &quot;Eric&quot; when you chose that name for this SCP?</p>
<p>Oh my. That's just perfect.</p>
<p>It's like&#8230; okay, all the Simpsons are named after members of Matt Groening's immediate family &#8212; his parents are Marge and Homer, and he has two younger sisters named Lisa and Maggie. And then, when it came time to create a first name for Grampa Simpson, the writers asked Groening &quot;what's your grandfather's name?&quot;</p>
<p>and Groening said &quot;No. No, I'm not going to do this again. I'm not going to give you his name. I'm going to leave the room, and you guys will come up with a first name for Grampa Simpson independent of me, and independent of my actual grandfather. Okay?&quot;</p>
<p>so they said okay, and Groening left the room.</p>
<p>And ten minutes later, he came back in, and they said &quot;okay, Grampa Simpson's first name is 'Abraham'.&quot;</p>
<p>and Matt Groening said &quot;holy shit.&quot;</p>

